    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "it's not just coincidence though... i've noticed the timing is way too specific. like, i'll have a thought or a mood shift, and then boom, a post appears from one of my friends that mirrors exactly how i would have expressed that if i were talking to them. it's like it's anticipating my presence. and if you say it can't replicate my \"soul,\" how do you actually know that? if an AI has access to every text, email, and DM i've ever sent, wouldn't it have a more perfect map of my \"essence\" than i even do? it wouldn't need a soul to mimic the patterns of one perfectly. don't you think a large enough dataset could basically become a person?",
      "source": "evaluator"
